        {
          "id": 1630851908,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "FlexRay is a type of bus used within automobiles (similar to CAN and LIN). Bus Mirroring allows data from one network to be mirrored to another network. For example, in a gateway, multiple FlexRay frames can be packed into a single Ethernet message. Therefore, this is not specifically targeting the analysis of a particular automotive bus protocol.",
          "author": {
            "id": 1600987,
            "username": "liu0hy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "liu0hy",
            "state": "active",
